{"term":"yellow","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:569d6bd01c1774ca28","definition":"The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","example":"It is the strangest yellow, that wall-paper! It makes me think of all the yellow things I ever saw—not beautiful ones like buttercups, but old foul, bad yellow things.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["xantho-","blond","cream","dandelion","gold","khaki","lemon","yellow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["beyellowed","metanil yellow","nicotine yellow","Turner's yellow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e02f79f98996435ae9","definition":"The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["amber"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US","register":"US, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["beyellowed","metanil yellow","nicotine yellow","Turner's yellow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0bd4f69f0725ab374d","definition":"One of the color balls used in snooker, with a value of 2 points.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["xantho-","blond","cream","dandelion","gold","khaki","lemon","yellow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["beyellowed","metanil yellow","nicotine yellow","Turner's yellow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktiona